\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Vermont\u8217 s supplemental food program for low-income women, infants and children, the first in the nation to be implemented statewide, began in 1974. It was the brainchild in part of Dr. Anthony Robbins, then one of the country\u8217 s youngest state health commissioners, at 33; he had secured a federal grant to made the program possible.}
